unts,\n   normalized domain/objective diagnostics, length, schedule ID, and model\n   family. Exclude exact witnesses, held-out labels, pair IDs, and any\n   feature that directly encodes correctness.\n3. Train a compact seeded KAN residual on calibration rows only. Compare a\n   constant baseline and size-matched MLP. Record every epoch and checkpoint\n   hash; do not tune on held-out metrics.\n4. Build local PWA lower and upper bounds per KAN unit. Allocate a fixed\n   global piece budget through unit-level dynamic programming and a\n   network-level knapsack. Record local and propagated error separately.\n5. Invoke the real MILP solver on finite feature bounds. Prove output bounds,\n   monotonicity only where preregistered, stability under irrelevant-field\n   perturbations, and that hard infeasibility remains outside the residual.\n   Solver timeout or unknown cannot become a certificate.\n6. Evaluate KAN, PWA abstraction, constant, and MLP on held-out rows once.\n   Report AUROC, calibration error, pairwise ranking accuracy, abstraction\n   disagreement, latency, parameter count, and uncertainty intervals.\n7. Set certified_pwa_energy_ready_score=1 only when the MILP path executed,\n   every claimed bound is proven, abstraction disagreement stays within its\n   certified envelope, and all held-out rows are terminal. Do not require a\n   positive held-out accuracy result to mark execution complete.\n8. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, artifact validation,\n   adversarial verification, row-consistency lint, and root-clutter checks.\n9. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific\n   principle per required field and certified_pwa_energy_ready_score;\n   preconditions_checked; inference_substrate\n   (calibration_only_kan_training_plus_pwa_milp_certification); duration_s;\n   source_artifact_hashes; random_seed; feature_schema; feature_rows;\n   split_isolation_rows; training_rows; checkpoint_hash; model_config;\n   model_parameter_count; pwa_unit_rows; piece_budget_rows;\n   local_error_bound_rows; propagated_error_bound_rows; milp_query_rows;\n   milp_solver_receipts; invariant_certificate_rows; rows;\n   per_candidate_rows; heldout_comparison_rows; abstraction_disagreement_rows;\n   latency_rows; certified_pwa_energy_ready_score;\n   pwa_energy_heldout_positive_score; reproducibility_checksum;\n   gate_check_summary with failed check, expected value, and observed value\n   for any blocked verdict; verifier_is_oracle (false); verdict_class\n   (positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial);\n   honest_verdict with a terminal prefix consistent with verdict_class.\n\nRun command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6977_certified_pwa_kan_energy.py --date {date}\nDo NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.\n",
