+      "prompt": "CONTEXT:\nCarnot's FR-11 requirement is continuous learning from verified outcomes,\nnot a write counter. Exp6967 froze a clean 24-event chronological constraint\nstream, but Exp6962 never ran its learning arms because model loading failed.\nOlder exact-slot and unready-stream reruns are retired. V611 uses a new\nselected schedule, post-outcome transactions, information separation, and\nrollback on the clean stream.\n\nWork at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.\n\nEXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:\n- {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md\n- {project_root}/research-program.md section Continuous Self-Learning\n- {project_root}/results/experiment_6973_lease_aware_gguf_runtime.json\n- {project_root}/results/experiment_6974_claim_provenance_duration_lint.json\n- {project_root}/results/experiment_6976_exact_candidate_certification.json\n- {project_root}/results/experiment_6967_certified_error_headroom_fixture.json\n- {project_root}/results/experiment_6962_queue_regulated_self_learning.json\n- {project_root}/results/experiment_5895_shortcut_safe_continuous_self_learning.json\n- {project_root}/python/carnot/learning/continual_constraint_memory.py\n- {project_root}/python/carnot/learning/constraint_policy_store.py\n- {project_root}/python/carnot/inference/sota_models.py\n- {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/continuous-learning/spec.md\n- {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/constraint-verification/spec.md\n- {project_root}/research-references.md V611 MARCH entry\n\nTASK:\nRun a chronological three-arm continuous-learning experiment in which exact\noutcomes can update a small constraint-policy memory only after each event.\nMeasure held-future utility, plasticity, stability, forgetting, state size,\nand rollback against frozen and read-only controls under matched live-model\nbudgets.\n\nCONCRETE STEPS:\n0. PRECONDITIONS: require lease_aware_runtime_ready_score=1,\n   fixture_admissibility_ready_score=1, selected_policy_ready_score=1, the\n   exact Exp6967 24-event stream and hashes, Qwen cache, Z3, a writable\n   transaction directory, and no later-outcome fields visible at time zero.\n   On failure, write blocked_transactional_constraint_self_learning with\n   gate_check_summary; external absence is blocked, not partial.\n1. Add REQ-LEARN-6978 and tests for chronological visibility, arm isolation,\n   post-outcome commit, journal durability, rollback, restart recovery,\n   matched budgets, no-future access, and bare downstream fields.\n2. Resolve cached_sota_pair(gpu_indices=(0, 1)) and select the exact\n   Qwen entry as MODEL_SPECS:\n   unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF. A legacy model may smoke-test plumbing but\n   cannot enter any comparison or readiness score.\n3. Freeze event order, selected base schedule, prompts, 128-token cap,\n   seed sequence, arm order rotation, exact evaluator, memory schema,\n   maximum memory size, and rollback threshold before the first live call.\n4. Run three matched arms on each of 24 events with fresh inference contexts:\n   frozen selected schedule; read-only initial memory; and transactional\n   post-outcome write memory. Use identical model, event, and token budgets.\n5. At event t, expose only predecessor records through t-1. Make the prompt\n   and raw completion durable, run the independent exact executor, then give\n   the writer only atomic error class, exact certificate digest, schedule\n   metadata, and outcome. Hide model confidence and all future labels.\n6. Journal each proposed memory update before commit. Apply it only after the\n   exact outcome. Evaluate a sealed replay window after each commit; roll\n   back if the preregistered safety score worsens, and prove recovery after\n   a forced interruption fixture.\n7. Measure per-event exact success, parse success, schedule chosen, memory\n   hit, write, commit, rollback, latency, and state bytes. Compute\n   chronological gain over read-only, plasticity on newly recurring error\n   classes, stability