+      "prompt": "CONTEXT:\nICLR 2026 Spilled Energy derives training-free adjacent-step logit-energy\nsignals for hallucination detection. Carnot's Exp2497 found AUROC 0.4903 and\ncorrelation -0.0221 on a different corpus, so the generic diagnostic is not\nestablished. Exp6975 changes the evidence surface by capturing sufficient\nlogit statistics around exact, span-localized ConstraintIR mappings from all\nthree current SOTA families. This is one final requalification attempt.\n\nWork at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.\n\nEXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:\n- {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md\n- {project_root}/results/experiment_6975_delayed_constraint_candidate_bank.json\n- {project_root}/results/experiment_6976_exact_candidate_certification.json\n- {project_root}/results/experiment_2497_phase4_spilled_energy.json\n- {project_root}/python/carnot/verification/spilled_energy.py\n- {project_root}/python/carnot/verification/semantic_energy.py\n- {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/hallucination-detection/spec.md\n- {project_root}/research-references.md V611 entry for arXiv:2602.18671\n\nTASK:\nRecompute spilled and marginalized energy on exact output spans, compare\nthem with entropy and top-probability controls on locked held-out rows, and\ndecide once whether this diagnostic requalifies. No model call, prompt\nretune, post-hoc pooling choice, or exact-verifier selection is allowed.\n\nCONCRETE STEPS:\n0. PRECONDITIONS: require candidate_bank_complete_score=1,\n   candidate_certification_complete_score=1, all sufficient energy-trace\n   fields, exact span offsets, held-out labels, all three model families,\n   and matching candidate hashes. On failure, write\n   blocked_spilled_energy_requalification with gate_check_summary.\n1. Add REQ-VERIFY-6980 and tests for the paper formulas, multi-token span\n   pooling, trace sufficiency, calibration/held-out separation, degenerate\n   class handling, bootstrap intervals, and prior-verdict retirement.\n2. Freeze formula variants, mean span pooling, directionality, calibration\n   thresholds, missing-step policy, family aggregation, and requalification\n   gate before reading held-out labels.\n3. Recompute spilled energy, marginalized energy, entropy, and top-token\n   probability from recorded selected-token logits and full-vocabulary\n   logsumexp values. Reject rows whose trace cannot reproduce exactly.\n4. Use calibration rows only for sign and threshold selection. Evaluate\n   error detection once on held-out rows overall and separately by model,\n   schedule, formulation family, and error class.\n5. Report AUROC, AUPRC, calibration error, paired ranking accuracy, bootstrap\n   intervals, coverage, and abstention for every signal. Keep all per-span\n   rows, including malformed and missing traces.\n6. Set spilled_energy_evaluation_complete_score=1 when all eligible rows are\n   terminal. Set spilled_energy_requalified_score=1 only if held-out AUROC\n   is at least 0.65, its interval excludes 0.50, and it beats both entropy\n   and top-probability controls with a paired interval above zero in at\n   least two model families.\n7. If the gate fails, emit a terminal null and explicitly retire this\n   diagnostic under retire_if_same_verdict. Do not propose another pooling,\n   prompt, or corpus retry from within the task.\n8. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, artifact validation,\n   adversarial verification, row-consistency lint, and root-clutter checks.\n9. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific\n   principle per required field and both\n   spilled_energy_evaluation_complete_score and\n   spilled_energy_requalified_score; preconditions_checked;\n   inference_substrate (deterministic_recorded_logit_energy_reducer);\n   duration_s; source_artifact_hashes; formula_config; calibration_rows;\n   rows; per_span_results; trace_reproduction_rows; heldout_metric_rows;\n   per_model_metric_rows; per_schedule_metric_rows;\n   per_form